SUMMARY:Jocelyn Bell Burnell Lecture "The Discovery of Pulsars"
DESCRIPTION:Professor Jocelyn Bell Burnell is a renown astrophysicist worldwide. In 1967\, she made the outstanding discovery of the existence of pulsars during her PhD in Astrophysics at Cambridge under the supervision of Antony Hewish. The discovery of pulsars\, that emit radio waves in the form of pulses at regular intervals\, opened a crucial new field of research in astrophysics. In 1974\, the Nobel Prize in\nhttps://indico.in2p3.fr/event/40486/
LOCATION:Amphitheater\, John W. Boyer Center\, 41\, rue des Grands Moulins\, 75013 Paris
